In article <9jsi3q$1al$1@kadath.deep.it>, Cthulhu <noone@nowhere.it> writes:
:I have a VAXstation 3100, I don't know which model it is.
:..."VAXserver 3100 Model 60"...

  That is not a VAXstation 3100, keyboard or not.  (For no good reason, 
  I've memorized most model names, and I cannot say I've ever heard of 
  a model 60 among the 3100 series VAXstation/VAXserver/MicroVAX boxes.)

  Look for the model number on the serial sticker, usually on the back
  or bottom of the box, often near the power connection.  Post it.

  Alternatively, the CPU model code -- usually KA* -- is normally displayed 
  when the system powers up and runs its diagnostics, and the various KA* 
  codes for the various processors are listed in the OpenVMS FAQ.  Post it.

