Right.  Your Celebris XL5100 is capable of running dual P166s if it
has a DEC part #54-24490-01 processor card with an attached voltage
regulator #54-24002-01.

The difference between the XL5100 and an Alpha XL-series computer is
simply the processor card with processor and the bracket which holds
the processor card in place.  That's it.  Everything else except the
tiny blue "badge" on the front panel is identical between the two. 

At this time I do not have any Alpha parts in stock.  I'll leave it to
others as to the advisability of converting the computer to run as an
Alpha.  Alpha XL systems came in 266, 300, 333, and 366Mhz versions,
if my memory is not faulty.

If you want pricing on any required parts to upgrade to a dual P166
with 512K external cache, let me know.  We have a few still available.


... Ben Myers

