You have an albatross on your hands.

White ALpha's were strictly to run Windows NT and cannot run Tru64 UNIX nor
OpenVMS.
The firmware in the units was modified to not build a HWRPB in memory, thus
prventing the OS at install time from being able to identify the machine.
This was done in the SROM, which is not a socketed device.
Some systems even had a specail version of the Alpha chip installed, that
could not be identified.

These machines will most likely happily install and run LINUX, without a
problem.

rtt



