Not quite true. If you have PWS...-a series white box Alpha, you can load the -au firmware
to get the srm console, needed for vms and tru64 support. You will need to plug in a
supported scsi controller and video card, but that's all there is to it. Have done that on
two machines here myself with no problem.

The machines that are a problem are the XL... series machines, which have no srm console
officially. However, the Alpha Server 400 series (very similar motherboard and case as the
XL series white box Alphas) do have an srm console and you may be able to load this or
similar bios to get the srm console support. The key thing is the SRM console. Without
that, you're sunk...

Chris


