All Alpha systems have had an SRM console and most have had an ARC or
AlphaBIOS console.

Machines that shipped without an SRM console had it softloaded serially, or
over ethernet or from floppy disk in manufacturing.

You see, the SRM console was the only scriptable console available and was
used for testing the CPU modules and the systems during manufacture.

The last noter as I suspected many people would have made the mistake,
equated SROM, to SRM and this is absolutely not the case.

To the last noter, please go back and read more carefully where I talk about
SROM and not about SRM.

However, you stand corrected, all Alpha systems manufactured to date, have
had SRM consoles, just some of them remain within the manufacturing walls.

