> I have a VAXstation 3100, I don't know which model it is.
> Since I boot it from serial console, it now reports itself as a
> "VAXserver 3100 Model 60", but I'd like to know which model it REALLY
> is.

At the console, type SHOW VERSION or SHOW CPU
or SHOW CONFIG. One of those will report the
cpu module type (which one works depends
on which machine you have).

A KA41-A is a MicroVAX 3100 Model 10 (or 20)
A KA41-D is a MicroVAX 3100 Model 10e (or 20e)
A KA42-A is a VAXstation 3100 Model 30 (or 40)
A KA42-B is a VAXstation 3100 Model 38 (or 48)
A KA43   is a VAXstation 3100 model 76
etc.

Antonio

