OpenVMS (no slash, mixed case, and the "Open" part is silent ;-)

... You're trying too hard!  I think it wants the SN: (AB01000U3E
above), but it doesn't really care.  The license code doesn't check
the SN or the SID.  This is just for the paperwork.

The important thing to remember is to also acquire the layered
product PAK's.  You'll almost certainly need some of them (UCX
for TCP/IP, DVNETEND and/or DVNETRTG for DECNET, DW-MOTIF for
DECWindows, and a variety of compiler licenses.)

Lots of people forget this part and then when they boot up their
shiny new VMS system, can't get it to do anything.

HTH

