have run into a rather big problem.

one of the cpu's died in one machine, but the data was needed, so a
colleauge of mine put the hard drives in the other machine for use by the
department.

I see it that the hard drives should be put back, and merely switch to the
uniprocessor kernel (linux), and it should be about the same as before
(only minus one processor), but my colleauge did not label the hard drives
(which ones were from this box?). So I'm swapping out disks until I get
the right ones in the right boxes, and before I could put the last HD in
the box missing a processor, I power down from the SRM bios, put the HD
in, and turn it back on...the fans spin up (and HD), the monitor comes out
of powersave, but only long enough to figure out its not getting a signal
and goes back into powersave. (the system acts exactly like this with both
processors removed on power-up). but I know the processor works, it is
fine alone in the other box. I've tried reseating the ram (2GB each),
unplugging the SCSI cables, swapping out the video card... I'm about taxed
after spending 11 hours in front of the machine or scouring newsgroups.
If I leave the system on for a long time (about 20 mins) the processor
doesn't feel as if its getting warm at all.  There are 2 sets of 3 led's
on the front edge of the board and they look kind of like this:

The pairs are always the same and there is one for each processor, here's
what my dead system's looks like:
|
 ] 	<labeled D11 PWRGOOD (off)
|
 ]*	<labeled D10 SROM    (on)
|
 ]	<labeled D9  DC_OK   (off)
|


And this is what my good working system's looks like:
|
 ]*	(on)
|
 ]*	(on)
|
 ]	(off)
|


from my hours of scouring the newsgroup archives, all I can come up with
even resembling this (fans on, no video) are dead battery's and bad RAM,
but no mention of the CPU problems or the LED's

I'll be happy to answer any questions if you feel I may have left
something out.

Thanks in advance.

