Just did a somewhat informal test printing a lot of text via the
DECLaser 5100 PostScript driver.  The printer DOES print a lot faster
using PostScript than when using the LaserJet 4 PCL driver.

Actually, I'm not surprised.  At the time DEC designed the printer, I
would imagine that PostScript compatibility was a major requirement
because PostScript was the de facto printing standard for the
non-Wintel world.  So I guess I'll switch my computer to use
PostScript as the default, rather than PCL.

Learn and learn... Ben Myers 

