What are you using for your system console?  Are you using a real terminal,
or are you using a PC running a terminal emulator (I guess there is a third
option that you've actually got a glass tube, keyboard and mouse hooked up).

If you're using the PC you should be able to just cut and paste the DCL into
the window.

If you're using the other two options, printout the license PAKs for the OS
and the networking stuff and very carefully type in the DCL.  My guess is
that you're using SYS$UPDATE:VMSLICENSE and getting a couple of the fields
mixed up.  It can be tricky if you're not used to be doing it, and there is
always the problem of fumble fingering something.

