One or two power supplies at the back? (IIRC
they are not redundant - the second one
is for the extra stack of disks). If you
have two power supplies, you obviously
need two power cords ... (I know it 
sounds obvious but you may have two supplies
and not realised!). They are also
individually switched, so both switches
must be on.

When you switch on at the back the AC OK light
should be lit and the fans should spin up.
If they don't, start by checking the power
lead and its fuse.

There is also a DC On/Off button on
the OCP at the front.

If the big fan does not spin up, the system
will shut down after a few seconds. The manual 
recommends using a torch to look to see
if the fan is spinning. It does not say
what to do (other than call field service)
if it is not spinning.

I'll go have a look at our AS2100 in
the office on Monday to see if there
is anything obvious.

