Brent Rice <Randall.Rice@Colorado.edu> writes:

>Could somebody give me an idea of how to set up one workstation to work
>off of directories of another workstation using ADVFS?  How do I make a
>volume of a fileset to be a fileset of another workstation?

it's called NFS.  basically you could create some shares of exported filesystems
in /etc/exports and turn nfs on and then mount these on your remote workstation.

i would advise you to do a bit more reading if you're not familiar with these concepts
before you turn things on as there are security implications (with possible loss
of data)

unless you are trying to do the above literally - i.e mount the same physical
disk on two machines, in which case the complexity level just went up a lot
and a lot more information would be needed.

regards,

