and Tandem systems (especially if you include their associated storage) were
generating most of the profit (which supported selling industry-standard
servers at near-cost in order to hold or gain market share - gee, where have
we seen *that* before?).

Add in the statement that Alpha sales suffered due to
GS-introduction-related component shortages and this hardly constitutes an
indictment against Alpha's current and future profitability (rather the
reverse) - and the numbers remain consistent with the conclusions I drew
previously from the 1999 report.

