that cutoff point (after which OPS really becomes necessary to achieve
any kind of scalability) is at CPU counts well into double digits.

And, of course, there *are* scenarios where OPS really does
make sense. What I'm saying is that many people for which such
a setup doesn't make sense seem to look at TPC-C numbers.

