In article <9j3vi1$muh$06$1@news.t-online.com>, "Christian Ritter" <christian.ritter@rz.uni-mannheim.de> writes:
> Hello
> 
> How can I boot a DEC 3000/800 from CD-Drive ?

By default the basic command is:

	BOOT DKA400

but additional bits may be required depending on the operating system
on the CD-ROM.  For VMS try:

	BOOT -fl 0,0 DKA400

You can use the SHOW DEVICE command to verify that DKA400 (the default)
is the name of the CD-ROM drive.

