guesstimate) it'll be rare because everybody will assume
some other guy is going to keep it.

For you people in-house, burn some CDs.  Do not rely on in-house
permanent storage facilities to "keep" the bits.  Their charter
will change as the corporation changes and/or cost-cutting closes
the facility.

Pay especial attention to the little control files or tools
that you use to do your job.  That stuff does not get on
a customer tape but, in itself, contains a lot of knowledge
in dealing with the bits you do ship.

Try to get the sources, the software they need for building, 
and the resultant libraries, EXEs, etc. in one place.  The
ordering biz is such that it all has to be separated.

