>all kinds of problems w.r.t. dealing with bad data.

>The details were _all_ in the timing.  

Nope.  The details are all in the architecture, specifically the coherence and
ordering architectures.  

There are a number of different ordering constraints that can be placed on a
memory system.  

1. Do reads have to take place in the order they were issued?  
2. Do writes have to take place in the order they were issued, even if to
different addresses? 

etc etc.  

These constraints are especially fun when there is a network fabric of some sort
between the issuer(s) and the memory.  :-)

