Actually, there are cache replacement algorithms (e.g. psuedo-
random replacement using the low bits of a cycle counter to
select the way) for which no amount of memory reads is
guaranteed to flush the cache.  But for implementations like
that (and IMHO for any competent implementation) the
processor should provide explicit cache flush operations.
