Ok, I'll bite with a few.

1.
Standard algorithm for cache flush on PPC is to zero out a cache sized
region at a scratch address then flash invalidate the cache.

2.
If you want to wing and a prayer it by having (device)DMA accessible
memory cacheable for performance reasons, you enforce software coherency
with an invalidate after the dma has gone underneath cache.

3.
Large temporaries on stack. Why leave them to be flushed out when
you can nuke em.

4.
Not exactly the same but code relocations are easier if you invalidate
the Icache.

etc...

