SGI did not ditch MIPS. SGI spun off MIPS as an independant company,
while retaining the high performance processor design team from the MIPS
division. SGI let go the team working on the processors targetted
more towards the embedded space. The high performance MIPS design team 
at SGI is, and always has, worked side by side with the system design team to 
deliver current and future generations of MIPS/IRIX systems. 

There was a wobble towards windows in some areas but thankfully the management
responsible for those decisions is now gone.

