> always hope for a VMS subsystem for Windows XP running on IA64.

The NT kernel has many attractive points, though some of the design could
stand for a bit of rearchitecting... particularly where there are flat bits
of namespace globally shared among all processes. They're built on a true
hierarchical object naming scheme (bits of which emerge into view under
Win32 as the registry and filesystems, for example) so that shouldn't be a
problem.

The big problem with NT is that the only practical way to get to it (at least
until they really release Interix, which is again appearing imminent) is via
the Win32 subsystem. Win32 is a horrible bodge on so many levels that it
hardly bares further discussion...

So a real VMS-style subsystem under NT would be a very interesting thing to
contemplate. Pity it won't happen.

