Or into the next level of cache. This is used in zSeries - first
level cache is write-through, second level is write back, and
shared among >1 processors. That's part of how a processor can
die without the whole system dying: Other processors have access
to what it changed in memory through the second level cache.

(Yes, the second level cache should be made bulletproof if this
is part of what you're using it for.)

