"Greg Pfister" <pfister@us.ibm.com> wrote in message
news:3B4B51FB.548A7545@us.ibm.com...

...

> Also: One thing I've never been quite clear on: Is VMS a complete
> kernel-level single system image? Another way to put it: Is the
> single-system aspect implemented *completely* at an OS level, so
> that all the name spaces used all the kernel calls are globalized
> across the cluster, with all that implies?

In case no one better-qualified to respond chooses to do so, I'll give it a
shot:

No.  VMS clusters were IIRC explicitly designed to accommodate SSI-like
management without requiring it.  E.g., it was considered desirable also to
allow system management at an individual node level for, e.g., user
authorization/authentication, while still being able to share storage and
the cluster interconnect (this obviously still required that the nodes trust
each other, but not that they trust each other's users).

- bill





