Greg Pfister wrote:
> [snip]
> Also: One thing I've never been quite clear on: Is VMS a complete
> kernel-level single system image?

No. Current VMS is a modular kernel. The concept of a system "image"
does not exist.

> Another way to put it: Is the
> single-system aspect implemented *completely* at an OS level, so
> that all the name spaces used all the kernel calls are globalized
> across the cluster, [snip]

No. Each node of a cluster is autonomous, but co-operates with the other
cluster nodes for such things as connection management (cluster
membership), distributed lock management, etc. 

The Galaxy architecture (multiple partitions within a single hardware
unit) begins to introduce the concept of galactic memory which can be
shared among partitions.

---

I hope this answers some of your questions. No way am I qualified to
answer the remaining questions you posed; however, given that they are
related to architectures foreign to VMS, odds are that they don't apply.

