S/390 uses write-through L1 and write-back (with coherency) L2.  This allows
L1 to be treated as throw-away lookaside when a processor (including L1) fails.
It also permits simple parity checking (as opposed to ECC for L2 and beyond).
There are articles in IBM Journal of Research and Development (Vol43 no5/6)
describing this setup.

Michel.


