>Why would write-back cache compromise data integrity?

In the context of gracefully recovering from a CPU failure (which I think
is next to impossible anyway without arbitration and CPUx2 or x3),
a failing CPU can't possibly write back the data aso it's lost so
the problem has become harder.

Whatever thread it is executing, it can still own data for any of
