This is exactly why GS320's aren't a good basis for BIG machines. If you
really are going to use all the cpu's on a single application, Ahmdahl
doesn't care that you have "pools" of good performance. The
comms between 32 processor "super-nodes" is what will limit you..
So why pay more?

> wildfire's I/O isn't good enough to meet the bisection bandwidth - wildfire

Consider a cubic 3d decomposed application, e.g. Solid state physics
simulations.
If you half a 1024 processor machine composed
of e.g. 4x4x2 GS320's into 2 4x4 halves (I'm being generous giving the
maximal area, rather than a 2x4) you end up with 16 times the interconnect speed of a
single GS320 (typically this would be some aggregate over multiple
links per GS). Note that bisection BW in the larger machine does NOT
depend on the intra-GS320 bandwidth but on the external interconnect
because you can always choose surfaces which do not cut an individual GS.

