Storing into an signed byte from something larger should check
(in hardware or software) that the top n-7 bits have the same
value.  Storing into an unsigned byte from something larger should
check (in hardware or software) that the top n-8 bits are zero.

Absent hardware support, the Ada compiler has to do it in software.


