All the middling to big wins of which I am aware are either the SC series,
basically ES4X + Quadrics or DS?0 + myrinet.

In these big systems customers have already written either pure message
passing or intra-node threaded+ inter-node message passing
codes, otherwise they wouldn't scale (or indeed run on anything but
Origins). Indeed many important customers will have SHMEM (supported
by Quadrics) from t3d/t3e days with perhaps even Alpha assembler, making
the SC series arguably the substitute t3f.

Very high cost 32 way NUMA nodes are a poor basis for a thousand processor
system. I don't know the list price, but you're probably looking at
over 32 Million for the 32 fully populated GS320's, BEFORE you buy the
(many ports aggregated per 32 way node) interconnect to support scaling
32x32Gflop nodes.

You might as well buy the interconnect and stick cheap and trivially
independent memory systems in it.

