I don't have the info on hand, but there is a rather confusing situation
with some of the systems.  I don't know if it applies to any of the 4100s
and if so, which ones.

While there are three serial port connectors on some systems, and these are
systems that have serial "remote console front panel" (my term), only two of
the serial ports can be connected at the same time to the operating system.
There is a micro of some sort (8051 class?) that manages all three serial
ports; based on setting made talking to that micro, various of the external
serial ports can be connected to the two internal serial ports that the
software sees.  To understand this, you need to carefully read the system
hardware "user manual".

Like I said, I'm not sure if this applies to your situation....




