competition.  Cheap desktop Vaxes then Alphas, PDP10's,
Unisys A-series boxes, etc might have worked.  The Sun and Apollo (then
HP and IBM) boxes made way to PC's.  They're tne next ones to go now.

My hope is the move to Intel ia64 sprouts a smart idea in the folks in
Compaq... The ability to run NT 64 bit apps on desktop Open/VMS  
workstations.

Finally DEC would have what they were promised in Alpha NT...

