Intel designed the 486 and the 860 around the same time, and
manufactured them with the same process.  Roughly speaking, the 860
was twice as fast as the 486.  (Yes, I know that overall system
performance depends on the rest of the system and the peripherals and
the operating system and the phase of the moon.)  The 860 certainly
had all sorts of problems as a system chip but it did what it did real
fast.

