In article <3B3EE059.5090706@spth.de>, Philipp Krause  <pkk@spth.de> wrote:
>
>> It is still very hard to multithread software and a lot of the existing
>> code isn't.
>
>I think the vast majority of software can be multithreaded. I've written
>a nibbles clone that uses up to 20 threads (2 Threads + 3 threads per 
>player). I think it would have been harder not to use multithreading.

The issue isn't whether you can add multithreading, but whether you
will get a significant performance gain by doing so.  All experience
is that very little software that is not written for parallelism (of
some sort) will gain much from multithreading.  Quite a lot can be
written to do so, but it requires skill and effort.


